libretro-dolphin-sysfiles
==========================

Installs the official "Dolphin.zip" system-files pack for libretro-dolphin,
built from the very same public sources and script that RetroArch's
"Core System Files Downloader" uses (libretro/libretro-system-files,
scripts/dolphin.sh):

    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/Sys/codehandler.bin
    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/Sys/GameSettings/**, Load/**,
    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/Sys/Resources/**, Shaders/**,
    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/Sys/Themes/**, Profiles/**,
    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/Sys/Wii/**, GC/dsp_rom.bin, fonts, ...
    <system_directory>/dolphin-emu/license.txt

This is what makes the core stop complaining about the missing
"codehandler.bin" / Dolphin.zip system files.

On this machine retroarch.cfg already has
    system_directory = "~/.config/retroarch/system"
(the other cores' packs -- mame, dc, Mupen64Plus, ... -- already live there),
so the package (installed under /usr/share/retroarch/system/) is mirrored
in with a single symlink -- same layout as the other cores:

    ln -s /usr/share/retroarch/system/dolphin-emu \
          ~/.config/retroarch/system/dolphin-emu

(If you ever prefer, instead of the symlink you can point
system_directory directly at /usr/share/retroarch/system.)

GameCube IPL.bin region ROMs are NOT included (upstream doesn't ship
them either). For GC games: obtain them from hardware you own and place
at ~/.config/retroarch/system/dolphin-emu/Sys/GC/<region>/IPL.bin
(e.g. GC/USA/IPL.bin).
